WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.200
The Game of Thrones season 6 trailer is finally
out, and combined with a bunch of promo stills

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.100
and hints from the books, we can predict a
lot of the big events of the upcoming season

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.060
– so let’s have a look.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:15.240
The trailer starts at the Wall, with the body
of Jon Snow, who is stabbed to death by his

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.500
fellow Night’s Watchmen at the end of the
last season and book.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.980
It looks like there’s a conflict over Jon’s
corpse – Davos uses Jon’s sword to fight

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.740
some Night’s Watchmen, and we see some Watchmen
trying to break through a locked door.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.100
We also see the red witch Melisandre lurking
around, and talking to Davos.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:36.100
It looks like the Watchmen are trying to stop
Mel doing something to Jon's body – probably

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.740
some magic that will lead to Jon's resurrection.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:43.200
There are heaps of hints for Jon's return
in the books and the show, and it's believed

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.470
that Jon's direwolf Ghost might be involved
– so it’s telling that we see the wolf

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.100
by Jon’s side in the trailer.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.920
Later we see a battle known as Bastardbowl
beginning, between the Boltons on one side,

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.770
and the other northmen, with wildlings down
from the Wall, on the other.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:03.090
Tormund is there, Ramsay is probably there,
and we even see someone who looks suspiciously

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.739
like Jon.

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:08.670
Also near Winterfell, we see Sansa and Theon
fleeing from the Boltons, and it looks like

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.680
they get caught by a Bolton man with dogs,
but then Brienne appears, kills the man, and

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.470
presumably saves them.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:18.600
Sansa later looks like she’s in a safe situation,
maybe with Brienne or the northmen, though

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.030
Littlefinger looks like he’s lurking up
there too, so she might end up with him.

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:28.170
Point is, Sansa, Theon, Brienne and Littlefinger
may also get caught up in this massive battle.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:32.530
There’ll certainly be deaths – maybe Tormund,
hopefully Ramsay – though it looks like

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:36.680
he’s got at least 20 good men here, so he’s
probably unstoppable.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:41.189
Anyway in Bravos, we see that Arya is still
blind, and spends some time begging as Blind

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:42.189
Beth.

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:45.049
She’s still at the House of Black and White,
though she seems to have a falling out with

00:01:45.049 --> 00:01:49.990
her magical assassin friends the Faceless
Men – one of them, the Waif, hits her, and

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:54.690
we later see Arya leaping off a rooftop – maybe
running away from the Waif.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:59.200
This might indicate that Arya leaves the Faceless
Men, maybe returning to Westeros where she

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.979
has some unfinished business.

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:06.110
Further east, the city of Meereeis left in
the hands of a dwarf, an ex-slave, and two

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:08.379
eunuchs, which sounds like the start to some
terrible joke.

00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:12.010
There’s a shot of an explosion at the Great
Pyramid, which maybe could be caused by the

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:15.549
Sons of the Harpy, who continue to resist
Dany’s rule.

00:02:15.549 --> 00:02:20.079
We also see Tyrion in some dark underground
location, which could be the Pyramid basement

00:02:20.079 --> 00:02:22.739
where two of Dany’s dragons are locked up.

00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:25.299
Maybe this is how the dragons get released…

00:02:25.299 --> 00:02:26.299
While Tyrion and co.

00:02:26.299 --> 00:02:29.999
try to keep things under control in Meereen,
Daario and Jorah head off to look for Dany,

00:02:29.999 --> 00:02:33.329
who was last seen flying out of the city on
Drogon’s back.

00:02:33.329 --> 00:02:37.019
One of Jorah’s fingernails has visibly gone
black, which indicates the spread of the nasty

00:02:37.019 --> 00:02:39.349
disease Jorah caught from the stone men in
Valyria.

00:02:39.349 --> 00:02:44.109
It’ll be interesting to see if anyone finds
out about his condition, which is both deadly,

00:02:44.109 --> 00:02:45.109
and contagious.

00:02:45.109 --> 00:02:49.529
Anyway, it looks like Dany is captured by
Dothraki, and we see her being taken what

00:02:49.529 --> 00:02:53.689
looks like Vaes Dothrak, a sort of a sacred
city to the Dothraki.

00:02:53.689 --> 00:02:57.349
So things might look bad for Dany, but she’s
got a Drogon ex machina coming her way, so

00:02:57.349 --> 00:02:58.559
she’ll probably be okay.

00:02:58.559 --> 00:03:03.510
By the time Jorah and Daario find her, she’ll
have made a bloody barbeque of her Dothraki

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:04.840
captors.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.040
Back in Westeros, we see a new player arrive
at the Iron Islands.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:13.189
A ship sails in on a stormy sea, bringing
in the infamous pirate Euron Greyjoy , who

00:03:13.189 --> 00:03:17.560
for some reason doesn’t have an eyepatch,
despite being, you know, the “Crow’s Eye”,

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.949
the quintessential badass pirate king, but
anyway.

00:03:20.949 --> 00:03:24.900
We see Euron standing on a bridge in a storm
which is probably where he kills his brother

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:28.989
Balon, which leads to the Kingsmoot, an election
of sorts where the ironborn choose their new

00:03:28.989 --> 00:03:30.169
King.

00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:35.419
This could be a really cool scene, with Aeron
Damphair, Yara or Asha Greyjoy, and the Crow’s

00:03:35.419 --> 00:03:39.419
Eye, duking it out, though sadly there’s
apparently no Victarion.

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:42.590
In King’s Landing, Jaime has an awkward
sort of a ‘honey, I’m home’ moment,

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.159
bringing the body of Mycrella back to Cersei.

00:03:45.159 --> 00:03:48.760
In the books, Jaime and Cersei are pretty
well broken up at this point, but here, they

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.469
catch up on some incest, and Jaime promises
to help her win back her power.

00:03:52.469 --> 00:03:56.699
Their enemies are the Faith – the High Sparrow
and his followers, who seem determined to

00:03:56.699 --> 00:03:59.859
bring down the Lannisters – "bring down
an empire".

00:03:59.859 --> 00:04:04.199
The faith seems to still have Margaery imprisoned,
and it looks like the Tyrells try to get her

00:04:04.199 --> 00:04:05.199
back.

00:04:05.199 --> 00:04:09.749
The wildcard in this conflict is Robert Strong,
the reanimated Gregor Clegane made by Qyburn

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.049
to serve Cersei.

00:04:11.049 --> 00:04:14.859
As an eight-foot tall monsterous zombie Mountain,
we can be pretty certain that Bobby Strong

00:04:14.859 --> 00:04:18.120
will wreck shit up this season – “I choose
violence”.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:23.000
But if rumours prove true, the silent giant
might be stopped by his brother the Hound,

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.919
returned from the grave.

00:04:24.919 --> 00:04:28.740
At the end of the trailer, we see Bran standing
in the snow, turning around and seeing the

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.330
Night King, the apparent leader of the white
walkers.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:35.449
This isn’t actually happening for realises,
it’s a sort of a vision – remember, Bran

00:04:35.449 --> 00:04:39.449
is hanging out with this creepy old tree-man
called the “three-eyed crow” a.k.a.

00:04:39.449 --> 00:04:40.849
Brynden Rivers a.k.a.

00:04:40.849 --> 00:04:44.669
“Bloodraven”, who's recently been recast,
and who’s teaching him to use the magic

00:04:44.669 --> 00:04:49.300
of the old gods, which involves seeing through
the eyes of weirwood trees across long distances

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.289
and even back in time.

00:04:51.289 --> 00:04:55.110
Bran uses this magic to have visions of the
present and the past, and so this thing with

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.400
the white walkers looks like one of those.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.900
What’s really exciting though, are these
shots of what looks to be the fight at the

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:05.289
Tower of Joy, an event that books readers
have been obsessing over for literally twenty

00:05:05.289 --> 00:05:07.750
years, ever since the first book came out.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:11.229
This is something that happened towards the
end of Robert’s Rebellion, a epic fight

00:05:11.229 --> 00:05:16.340
with a young Eddard Stark and six of his men
against three famous Kingsguard knights, including

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:17.990
the legendary Arthur Dayne.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:22.909
But more important than the fight is its aftermath,
where Eddard makes a promise to his dying

00:05:22.909 --> 00:05:27.150
sister Lyanna – which is believed to relate
to birth of Jon Snow.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:30.689
This scene could lead to the reveal of one
of the biggest, oldest secrets in Game of

00:05:30.689 --> 00:05:34.710
Thrones – the true parentage of Jon Snow
– R+L=J.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:35.710
So that’s the trailer.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:39.600
You got the resurrection of Jon Snow, your
Bastardbowl, Arya going rogue, and conflict

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:40.600
in Meereen.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:44.960
You got your Dothraki BBQ, your Kingsmoot,
possibly Cleganebowl, and finally, after all

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:47.099
these years, the Tower of Joy.

00:05:47.099 --> 00:05:51.520
This season looks like it's gonna be great,
so make sure to subscribe for more explanations

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.189
and analysis throughout the series.

00:05:53.189 --> 00:05:57.509
We’ve already got videos out on Arya’s
character arc, Dany’s future path, greyscale,

00:05:57.509 --> 00:06:02.430
Euron Greyjoy, Robert Strong, the return of
the Hound, R+L=J, Jon's resurrection, and

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:05.969
much more, so check those out if you’re
keen, and expect many more videos throughout

00:06:05.969 --> 00:06:08.150
Season 6 and beyond.

